IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc27-length`
IMPORT `ccc27-s748-pardons-disabilities`

-- ccc27-tests-s748.l4 -- tests for sections 748 to 751.1. Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion.

§ `Tests -- sections 748 to 749`

#ASSERT `s 748(1) Her Majesty may extend the royal mercy to the person, even if the person is imprisoned for failure to pay money to another person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 748(1) Her Majesty may extend the royal mercy to the person, even if the person is imprisoned for failure to pay money to another person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 748(2) the Governor in Council may grant the pardon` TRUE `s 748(2) a free pardon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 748(2) the Governor in Council may grant the pardon` TRUE `s 748(2) a conditional pardon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 748(2) the Governor in Council may grant the pardon` TRUE `s 748(2) a pardon of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 748(2) the Governor in Council may grant the pardon` FALSE `s 748(2) a free pardon` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a person convicted of an offence
#ASSERT `s 748(3) the person is deemed thereafter never to have committed the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 748(3) the person is deemed thereafter never to have committed the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no free pardon granted ("Where")
#ASSERT `s 748(3) the person is deemed thereafter never to have committed the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another offence than the one pardoned
#ASSERT `s 748(4) the pardon prevents or mitigates the punishment to which the person might otherwise be lawfully sentenced on the subsequent conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "No free pardon or conditional pardon prevents or mitigates"
#ASSERT `s 748(4) the pardon prevents or mitigates the punishment to which the person might otherwise be lawfully sentenced on the subsequent conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a conviction for the offence pardoned
#ASSERT `s 748(4) the pardon prevents or mitigates the punishment to which the person might otherwise be lawfully sentenced on the subsequent conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 748.1(1) the Governor in Council may order the remission, in whole or in part, of the fine or forfeiture` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 748.1(1) the Governor in Council may order the remission, in whole or in part, of the fine or forfeiture` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 748.1(2) the order for remission may include the remission of the costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 748.1(2) the order for remission may include the remission of the costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "no costs to which a private prosecutor is entitled shall be remitted"
#ASSERT `s 748.1(2) the order for remission may include the remission of the costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 749 the provision limits or affects Her Majesty's royal prerogative of mercy` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Nothing in this Act ... limits or affects"
#ASSERT `s 749 the provision limits or affects Her Majesty's royal prerogative of mercy` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 750`

`s 750 test 2 years` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
`s 750 test 2 years less a day` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`
`s 750 test other offence` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 334, ""

-- (1): an indictable offence, two years or more, holding an office at the time
#ASSERT `s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` TRUE `s 750 test 2 years` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` TRUE `imprisonment for life` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` TRUE `s 750 test 2 years less a day` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- under two years
#ASSERT `s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` TRUE `no imprisonment is stated` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no term stated
#ASSERT `s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` FALSE `s 750 test 2 years` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not convicted of an indictable offence
#ASSERT `s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` TRUE `s 750 test 2 years` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- holds no office at the time
-- (2): args: subsection (1) applies; the capacity; undergone the punishment; free pardon
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST TRUE) `s 750(2) holding any office under the Crown or other public employment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST TRUE) `s 750(2) being elected as a member of Parliament or of a legislature` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST TRUE) `s 750(2) sitting or voting as a member of Parliament or of a legislature` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST TRUE) `s 750(2) exercising any right of suffrage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST TRUE) `s 750(2) exercising any right of suffrage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "until" bar: the punishment has been undergone
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST TRUE) `s 750(2) exercising any right of suffrage` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a free pardon
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST TRUE) `s 750(2) another capacity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` (JUST FALSE) `s 750(2) exercising any right of suffrage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- subsection (1) does not apply
#ASSERT `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` NOTHING `s 750(2) exercising any right of suffrage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): args: convicted; the offence; section 380 against Her Majesty; Financial Administration Act offence
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 121, "(1)") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) section 121
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 124, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 418, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 380, "(1)") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) section 380 against Her Majesty
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 380, "(1)") FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 380 not against Her Majesty
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` TRUE `s 750 test other offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c) the Financial Administration Act
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` TRUE `s 750 test other offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 121, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not convicted
-- (4) to (6)
#ASSERT `s 750(4) the person may apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of one or more of the capacities lost` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(4) the person may apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of one or more of the capacities lost` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "at any time before a record suspension ... is ordered"
#ASSERT `s 750(4) the person may apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of one or more of the capacities lost` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- subsection (3) does not apply
#ASSERT `s 750(5) the Governor in Council may order that the capacities lost be restored, in whole or in part, subject to conditions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(5) the Governor in Council may order that the capacities lost be restored, in whole or in part, subject to conditions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- conditions not such as the Governor in Council considers desirable
#ASSERT `s 750(5) the Governor in Council may order that the capacities lost be restored, in whole or in part, subject to conditions` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application under subsection (4) ("Where")
#ASSERT `s 750(6) subsection (6) removes any disability imposed by section 750` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 750(6) subsection (6) removes any disability imposed by section 750` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- sections 751 to 751.1`

#ASSERT `s 751 the person in whose favour judgment is given is entitled to recover costs from the opposite party` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 751 the person in whose favour judgment is given is entitled to recover costs from the opposite party` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not proceedings by indictment for defamatory libel
#ASSERT `s 751 the person in whose favour judgment is given is entitled to recover costs from the opposite party` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- judgment not in the person's favour
#ASSERT `s 751 the costs are in a reasonable amount to be fixed by order of the court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 751 the costs are in a reasonable amount to be fixed by order of the court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 751 the costs are in a reasonable amount to be fixed by order of the court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 751.1 the party in whose favour judgment is given may enter judgment for the amount of the costs` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 751.1 the party in whose favour judgment is given may enter judgment for the amount of the costs` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no filing in a civil court with jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 751.1 the party in whose favour judgment is given may enter judgment for the amount of the costs` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- costs not fixed under section 751 ("Where")
#ASSERT `s 751.1 the party in whose favour judgment is given may enter judgment for the amount of the costs` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the costs were paid forthwith
#ASSERT `s 751.1 the judgment is enforceable against the opposite party as if it were a judgment rendered against that party in civil proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 751.1 the judgment is enforceable against the opposite party as if it were a judgment rendered against that party in civil proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
